    "description": "<p data-local-id=\"45fbad70f698\"><strong>To Do: </strong></p><ul data-local-id=\"2d45a2565deb\"><li data-local-id=\"85458deda1bc\"><p data-local-id=\"ff250b567e2f\">Wagertech provided mockups for the Affiliate Link creation and management so they can create them in larger batches rather than one record at a time. </p></li><li data-local-id=\"ad8dcd592045\"><p data-local-id=\"ceaf6fa5dbc8\">Review the mockup <a href=\"https://deal-management.netlify.app/link-modal\" data-card-appearance=\"inline\">https://deal-management.netlify.app/link-modal</a>  </p></li><li data-local-id=\"8b369b5abe98\"><figure data-local-id=\"2d44adea5551\" data-type=\"media-single\" data-layout=\"align-start\" data-width=\"527\" data-width-type=\"pixel\"><div data-type=\"media\" data-media-type=\"file\" data-id=\"25638b5d-f6f1-4769-b76e-7beab0a7612d\" data-alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-22 at 10.29.37 AM.png\" data-width=\"1104\" data-height=\"554\"></div></figure><p data-local-id=\"ec793c1de86c\"></p></li><li data-local-id=\"e43a7bec8845\"><p data-local-id=\"e34f19e1f2e8\">Click on Edit Links for the desired behaviour for the popup</p><ul data-local-id=\"63982105c914\"><li data-local-id=\"4b1852271570\"><p data-local-id=\"6fb79cd7818d\">Run a research spike and evaluate the feasibility of building a screenflow to reproduce the behaviour in the mockup. </p></li><li data-local-id=\"2795ebe5b33f\"><p data-local-id=\"4600d74310f7\">Timebox the investigation to 2-3 hours (unless building a POC) </p></li></ul></li><li data-local-id=\"9962d880705c\"><p data-local-id=\"b238f5c1f7b7\"><strong>Additional Requirements: </strong></p><ul data-local-id=\"6372b0ade647\"><li data-local-id=\"1322fa099643\"><p data-local-id=\"5eb79c920c5e\">Deleting links via this interface should require a confirmation step, so the <code>x</code> next to the link isn’t necessary for now. However, if it’s possible to pop up a confirmation for the deletion when they click the <code>x</code> without disrupting the rest of the screenflow, then let’s keep it in the design. </p></li><li data-local-id=\"a6da644b5be0\"><p data-local-id=\"7978ec3d842c\">Trigger a sync to CMS when Affiliate Links Edited</p><ul data-local-id=\"476e2949bd42\"><li data-local-id=\"c74d8e833817\"><p data-local-id=\"f4ceeaffa1e7\">Create a checkbox on the related Deal object called “Affiliate Links Edited” that should be set to true when the following occurs during the Edit Links process:</p><ul data-local-id=\"18b7be50128b\"><li data-local-id=\"c4d437228452\"><p data-local-id=\"dd6ea3945147\">New affiliate link is added</p></li><li data-local-id=\"7afbfb65906d\"><p data-local-id=\"a2465bd6318e\">Existing affiliate link is removed</p></li><li data-local-id=\"e2bbc0142d7a\"><p data-local-id=\"e94d7cd035a6\">Link status is changed (Active &lt;&gt; Inactive)</p></li><li data-local-id=\"b1d4a00583ff\"><p data-local-id=\"b3d62ee3b6b7\">Link URL is changed</p></li><li data-local-id=\"db55a56a47f2\"><p data-local-id=\"e97dd0481228\">Link Code is changed</p></li><li data-local-id=\"3ae985c9f78d\"><p data-local-id=\"95b34ad6320a\">Link Cap is changed</p></li></ul></li><li data-local-id=\"96c1324dee88\"><p data-local-id=\"5170ac961f1b\">If a user clicks Edit links but no changes are made, then this checkbox should remain unchecked (or whatever state it was in prior to the link being edited) </p></li><li data-local-id=\"13c10f58b310\"><p data-local-id=\"a6cad965c241\">This checkbox will then be used to drive a separate automation that triggers a sync to the CMS to send the updated Link information to CMS. (Not scoped yet, but is part of the requirements we received from them in this scope document: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/home\">https://drive.google.com/drive/home</a> )</p></li></ul></li></ul></li></ul><p data-local-id=\"ad499a118c16\"></p><p data-local-id=\"b5b58849ffbb\"></p><h1 data-local-id=\"51df584f4acb\">Original Ticket Notes: (for historical reference) </h1><hr data-local-id=\"347504c1afc5\"><p data-local-id=\"9f3c3fcd5644\"> AL-4: Link Editing (Screen Flow)</p><p data-local-id=\"3625d581d5ff\">Build the editing experience for Link records as a screen flow rather than a standard record-edit modal.</p><p data-local-id=\"7b23f2d4c250\">AUTOMATION</p><p data-local-id=\"0618cb97e0b0\">Editing actions for this object (e.g., the Edit Links modal) will be built as Screen Flows, not standard record-edit modals.</p><p data-local-id=\"018039f1bf8a\">IMPLEMENTATION REQUIREMENTS</p><p data-local-id=\"df2fad1538ba\">The Deal object itself needs no further story work — remaining build work lives on the Link/Affiliate Link object.</p><p data-local-id=\"35ea71d4e7a1\">A &quot;Path&quot; (progression status bar) component exists on at least one WagerTech record page today but isn&#039;t in any prototype — remove it wherever it appears, including here if present. Not confirmed which record page(s) currently show it — check before building.</p><p data-local-id=\"1e0bb78f5c66\">NOTES</p><p data-local-id=\"0a3ceab02259\">Provenance: AL-4 (Affiliate Link Record User Stories doc).</p><p data-local-id=\"b8b3dbaa9d34\">Actual flow build is expected to be done by Cedric or Chester per Kobi — this ticket scopes the requirement, not necessarily the builder.</p><p data-local-id=\"0a2c08342fed\">SOURCE</p><p data-local-id=\"12a3a8cf2a2c\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MsJXwt3oY-DyQuAdMzNYlyPenKUQl7g8mHzMmeRaVHs/edit?tab=t.nyoinaymgezg\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MsJXwt3oY-DyQuAdMzNYlyPenKUQl7g8mHzMmeRaVHs/edit?tab=t.nyoinaymgezg</a></p><p data-local-id=\"2a35e92e583f\">Aug 19, 2026 Kobi/Taryn Daily Sync — not confirmed via Fathom; no recording of this meeting was found in the connected account. Sourced from Taryn&#039;s own documentation of that conversation, not from an independently checked transcript.</p><p data-local-id=\"456c468edd56\">Dependencies: <a href=\"https://app.asana.com/0/0/1217693636693194/f/\">BUILD-220 — Affiliate Link: Link Core Fields</a></p><p data-local-id=\"968812c0fc4c\">Owner (proposed): Taryn Reithofer</p><p data-local-id=\"fa0f4ead10c0\">Created 2026-08-20 from Affiliate Link record documentation review.</p>",
